Z||000000||maryjane||06-28-2001||08:09 PM||||My dialup connection is always about the same, fairly fast, but about once a week, it takes forever to load my home page, or any other,even this forum. When I type in a url or click on a link, the taskbar says "finding site" and the blue bar starts stringing out like it always does, but nothing else happens,eventually,I get the hated "cannot display page". A few hours or sometimes minutes, everything works fine.Is it just athe amount of people trying to use the web or do I have a problem with my computer?<BR>233mz<BR>64 meg ram<BR>Earthlink 5.0/ie5.0<BR>56k modem<BR>plenty of video ram<BR>Thanks in advance<BR>Don<P>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 06-28-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 06-28-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Jake_Dragon||06-28-2001||08:42 PM||||Check to see if there is a second number you can use, check and see if earthlink has alternative DNS settings. I just went to Road Runner and it is the best!!||||reg||1
