Z||000009||LarryB||06-29-2001||05:37 PM||||You should be able to use a laptop, as long as you've got an Ethernet card installed. The computer connects to the cable modem via an Ethernet cable so as long as you use a card supported by your OS it shouldn't be a problem.<P>Or, you could get a docking station to use when you want RR connectivity and remove the laptop when you want to use dialup.<P>There is a pattern to when you're more likely to have connectivity problems.  The general trend of Internet traffic pattern in the US is roughly:<P>- at its lowest usage 4-6AM  daily (Eastern)<BR>- most scheduled maintenance is done between 3AM-6AM Eastern (chicken and egg, its done now because traffic is at its lightest, traffic is at its lightest in part because parts of the network are offline for maintenance)<BR>- at its highest 7-11PM daily (Eastern) <BR>- The highest traffic peak is on Sunday or   <BR>Monday night.  The peak each successive <BR>night is lower than the peak of the night <BR>before, and the peak is at its lowest Saturday night.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>You think dial up is bad.....try webtv   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>I dont have dsl in the area yet, and Roadrunner has to have a component installed in cmpt, and I have laptop. I say (even though im told not) that its just because of all the computers online now.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Jake_Dragon||06-29-2001||05:43 PM||||My old provider "GTE" change the DNS server addresses and made everything slow. As soon as I configured the new addresses in everything was faster.||||reg||1
Z||000011||theogre||06-29-2001||08:31 PM||||Earthlink auto assigns DNS on login. so that should not be an issue.<P>Earthlink is under construction in some markets. This may be part of you slowdown.<P>Getting a fast dial connection doesn't mean the network is ok. I just means that a slot was free for you to dial into. Earthlink has had sporadic problems with some of it's boarder gateways to the "internet cloud" for some time. These problems can effect the whole earthlink network or just certain POP's.<P>Next time the system seems slow see of you can hit <A HREF="http://www.earthlink.com" TARGET=_blank>www.earthlink.com</A> <P>Also, learn how to use Tracert and Ping. These will tell you just where the problem is on the network or on the global internet.||||reg||1
Z||000012||maryjane||06-29-2001||11:57 PM||||Thanks for all the suggestions. Strangely enough, we got an email from earthlink support today (spyware?)explaining some construction going on with them. Also heard their rates will be going up.<BR>Don & Jane||||reg||1
